t":"Status reporting"},{"text":"Resource planning"},{"text":"Meeting summaries"},{"text":"Engineering documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Growing areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital twins"},{"text":"Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE)"},{"text":"Simulation"},{"text":"Digital thread"},{"text":"Requirements traceability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI Engineering Programmes"},{"type":"p","text":"TPMs increasingly need to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI infrastructure"},{"text":"GPU systems"},{"text":"Data pipelines"},{"text":"Model lifecycle"},{"text":"MLOps"},{"text":"AI safety"},{"text":"Model evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Autonomous Engineering Workflows"},{"type":"p","text":"AI agents may increasingly coordinate parts of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Requirement","Planning","Development","Testing","Deployment","Monitoring"]},{"type":"p","text":"The TPM's role will increasingly shift toward technical decision-making, risk governance, cross-functional alignment, and strategic execution."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Systems Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Technical Architecture"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Requirements Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Software / Cloud Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Agile & Programme Management"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Risk & Dependency Management"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Product Thinking"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Stakeholder Management"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Jira + Confluence"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Excel + Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"SQL + Python"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Cloud Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Technical Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Leadership"}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Understand system architecture and engineering lifecycles"},{"text":"Write and manage technical requirements"},{"text":"Create programme roadmaps"},{"text":"Build project schedules and milestones"},{"text":"Identify technical dependencies"},{"text":"Maintain risk and issue registers"},{"text":"Use Jira and Confluence effectively"},{"text":"Understand Agile/Scrum delivery"},{"text":"Read basic architecture diagrams"},{"text":"Understand APIs, databases, cloud and DevOps"},{"text":"Build management dashboards"},{"text":"Communicate with engineers and business stakeholders"},{"text":"Lead a multidisciplinary technical project"},{"text":"Complete at least one substantial engineering internship"},{"text":"Demonstrate both technical depth and delivery leadership"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Systems Engineer","Technical Programme Manager","Product/Technology Leader"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the most important principle is “technical credibility before management title.” A B.Tech graduate should first become strong enough technically to understand engineering decisions, then progressively take ownership of cross-team delivery, risks, dependencies and strategic programmes."}]}]}